@startuml

title 11.1. Universal status transition service architecture

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

interface WorkflowSubjectInterface {
	+ getWorkflowKey(): string
	+ getStatusValue(): string
	+ setStatusValue(status: string): void
}

class TransitionContext <<value object>> {
	+ actor: User?
	+ source: string
	+ occurredAt: DateTimeImmutable
	+ comment: string?
	+ payload: array
	+ correlationId: string?
}

class TransitionResult <<value object>> {
	+ entity: object
	+ transitionKey: string
	+ fromStatus: string
	+ toStatus: string
}

class StatusTransitionService <<service>> {
	+ apply(subject, transitionKey, context): TransitionResult
	+ can(subject, transitionKey, context): bool
}

class WorkflowRegistry <<registry>> {
	+ getFor(subject): WorkflowDefinitionInterface
}

interface WorkflowDefinitionInterface {
	+ supports(subject): bool
	+ getTransition(key): TransitionDefinition
	+ getHistoryRecorder(): HistoryRecorderInterface
}

class TransitionDefinition <<value object>> {
	+ key: string
	+ fromStatuses: string[]
	+ toStatus: string
	+ guards: TransitionGuardInterface[]
	+ beforeActions: TransitionActionInterface[]
	+ afterActions: TransitionActionInterface[]
	+ historyEventKey: string
}

interface TransitionGuardInterface {
	+ assertAllowed(subject, transition, context): void
}

interface TransitionActionInterface {
	+ execute(subject, transition, context): void
}

interface HistoryRecorderInterface {
	+ record(subject, transition, context, result): void
}

class DomainEventDispatcher <<service>> {
	+ dispatch(event): void
}

class OrderWorkflowDefinition <<definition>>
class PurchaseWorkflowDefinition <<definition>>
class InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition <<definition>>
class ProductionOrderWorkflowDefinition <<definition>>

class OrderHistoryRecorder <<history>>
class GenericStatusHistoryRecorder <<history>>

class OrderHasEntriesGuard <<guard>>
class NoPostedDocumentsGuard <<guard>>
class NoPaymentsGuard <<guard>>

class ReserveStockAction <<action>>
class ReleaseReservationsAction <<action>>
class RecalculateProgressAction <<action>>

WorkflowSubjectInterface <|.. Order
WorkflowSubjectInterface <|.. Purchase
WorkflowSubjectInterface <|.. InventoryDocument
WorkflowSubjectInterface <|.. ProductionOrder

StatusTransitionService --> WorkflowRegistry : resolve workflow
StatusTransitionService --> TransitionContext : uses
StatusTransitionService --> TransitionResult : returns
StatusTransitionService --> DomainEventDispatcher : dispatch after commit
WorkflowRegistry --> WorkflowDefinitionInterface : returns
WorkflowDefinitionInterface --> TransitionDefinition : exposes
TransitionDefinition --> TransitionGuardInterface : checks
TransitionDefinition --> TransitionActionInterface : before/after pipeline
WorkflowDefinitionInterface --> HistoryRecorderInterface : selects

WorkflowDefinitionInterface <|.. OrderWorkflowDefinition
WorkflowDefinitionInterface <|.. PurchaseWorkflowDefinition
WorkflowDefinitionInterface <|.. InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition
WorkflowDefinitionInterface <|.. ProductionOrderWorkflowDefinition

HistoryRecorderInterface <|.. OrderHistoryRecorder
HistoryRecorderInterface <|.. GenericStatusHistoryRecorder

TransitionGuardInterface <|.. OrderHasEntriesGuard
TransitionGuardInterface <|.. NoPostedDocumentsGuard
TransitionGuardInterface <|.. NoPaymentsGuard

TransitionActionInterface <|.. ReserveStockAction
TransitionActionInterface <|.. ReleaseReservationsAction
TransitionActionInterface <|.. RecalculateProgressAction

OrderWorkflowDefinition --> OrderHistoryRecorder : order timeline
PurchaseWorkflowDefinition --> GenericStatusHistoryRecorder : generic status history
InventoryDocumentWorkflowDefinition --> GenericStatusHistoryRecorder : generic status history
ProductionOrderWorkflowDefinition --> GenericStatusHistoryRecorder : generic status history

note right of StatusTransitionService
  Stable orchestration core.

  Responsibilities:
  1. Resolve workflow definition by subject.
  2. Resolve transition by key.
  3. Check current status is allowed.
  4. Run guard pipeline.
  5. Run before-actions.
  6. Change status.
  7. Run after-actions.
  8. Delegate history recording.
  9. Dispatch domain event.

  It must not contain entity-specific if/else branches.
  New entities and new transitions are added through definitions
  and handlers, not by editing this service.
end note

note right of TransitionDefinition
  Use named transitions, not direct status assignment.

  Example:
  - confirm: draft -> confirmed
  - return_to_draft: confirmed -> draft

  Forward and backward transitions are separate business rules.
  A reverse transition is not automatically the mirror of forward one.
end note

note right of WorkflowDefinitionInterface
  Per-entity extension point.

  A workflow definition owns:
  - allowed transitions for one subject type
  - selected guards/actions
  - history recorder choice

  Future entities plug in by adding a new definition class
  and registering it in WorkflowRegistry.
end note

note right of HistoryRecorderInterface
  History strategy extension point.

  - OrderHistoryRecorder writes rich OrderHistory timeline rows.
  - GenericStatusHistoryRecorder writes StatusHistory rows
    for Purchase, InventoryDocument and ProductionOrder.

  The core transition service does not know which table is used.
end note

note bottom
  Execution pipeline:

  apply(subject, transitionKey, context)
    -> workflowRegistry.getFor(subject)
    -> definition.getTransition(transitionKey)
    -> guards.assertAllowed(...)
    -> begin transaction
    -> beforeActions.execute(...)
    -> subject.setStatusValue(toStatus)
    -> afterActions.execute(...)
    -> historyRecorder.record(...)
    -> commit
    -> dispatch domain event

  can(...) runs the same resolution and guard checks,
  but never mutates the subject.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation rules:

  1. Prefer explicit handler classes over anonymous callbacks
     for business rules that matter.
  2. Builder/DSL may be used only to assemble definitions cleanly.
  3. Keep workflow definitions declarative;
     put heavy business logic into guard/action services.
  4. Keep transition keys stable once exposed to UI/API.
  5. Every direct status write outside the service should be treated
     as a bug unless it is object construction/default initialization.
  6. Add tests at three levels:
     - definition graph tests
     - guard/action unit tests
     - service integration tests with history assertions.
end note

@enduml
